<title>USA: Morgan Stanley to elevate Joseph Perella - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Morgan Stanley to elevate Joseph Perella - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>After little more than three years at Morgan Stanley &amp; Co, the firm is expected to promote 1980s merger star Joseph Perella to head its investment banking group, The Wall Street Journal reported Thursday.</p>
<p>Perella had joined the firm in November, 1993, as a senior deal maker, the story said.</p>
<p>The Journal said the appointment is part of a broader reorganization that could be announced as early as Thursday.</p>
</text>
